        "answer": "# Fundamental Duties\n\nFundamental Duties are moral obligations enshrined in the Constitution of India, intended to promote a spirit of patriotism and uphold the unity of India. These duties are not enforceable by law but serve as a reminder to citizens of their responsibilities towards society and the nation.\n\nThey were added to the Constitution by the **42nd Amendment Act of 1976** based on the recommendations of the **Swaran Singh Committee**. Originally ten in number, the **86th Amendment Act of 2002** added an eleventh duty concerning education.\n\nSome key Fundamental Duties include:\n1) To abide by the Constitution and respect its ideals and institutions, the National Flag and the National Anthem.\n2) To cherish and follow the noble ideals which inspired our national struggle for freedom.\n3) To uphold and protect the sovereignty, unity and integrity of India.\n4) To defend the country and render national service when called upon to do so.\n5) To promote harmony and the spirit of common brotherhood amongst all the people of India."
